EXTENSION "ARMDef_Against_the_Dark_TheBulgarians_BenildaOfGuernicus" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, Against the Dark - Benilda of Guernicus"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_Against_the_Dark_Core_Ext"

    # Benilda of Guernicus (Chapter Four: The Bulgarians, p55): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #tb48c4d0a2843bbe37c1b13 ^"Benilda of Guernicus" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t7219cfed18368b3394b4bd ^"Seuthopolis"]
            ^"Age" STRING "78 Personality traits: Assertive +3, Stubborn +2. Specializes in investigation. Privilege: Soci"
            ^"Source" STRING "Against the Dark"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 55
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Benilda is the chief Quaesitor of the Transylvanian Tribunal. She is one of the leaders of the Transitionalist Movement within House Guernicus. She believes that the Tremere may be correct: the way magi live will change in future. This will pose great challenges to those charged with meting out justice. Benilda is a legal innovator, who hopes to prepare her House for the challenges ahead.\n\nThis view does not make her popular with the Traditional faction of House Guernicus. They see her style of Transitionalism as collaboration with House Tremere to corrupt the Code. There is very little they can do to her, however — she has the support of House Tremere. Without the military aid of House Tremere, the Quaesitores might find it difficult to force Autumn covenants, in some other Tribunals, to abide by the Code.\n\nThe current Prima of Guernicus has tried to make peace between the Traditional and Transitional factions by noting that their battles will be won not through intramural debate, but on the floors of various Tribunal meetings. Benilda thinks that abandoning internal conciliation was weak and silly. She accepts, however, that her rivals have been told by their leader to abandon conciliation and fight public battles, Tribunal by Tribunal, case by case. Given that she has no choice, and that the future of the Order is at stake, Benilda is willing to play political games just as savage as any of her Traditional sodales.\n\nBenilda is the Quaesitor characters are most likely to see when they require assistance with the administrative elements of the Tribunal’s culture. She is the Quaesitor who presides at Tribunals and, while there, witnesses oaths and binds contracts into the Peripheral Code. She is also the person before whom they accuse others of crimes, to trigger investigations."
    }

}
